@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site. Deploy behind HTTPS for local network access;
+localhost is a secure-context exception for development. A public HTTP deployment
+cannot request local network permissions.
+
+The local resource form reads a user-supplied HTTP or HTTPS endpoint on a LAN
+device or loopback service. It queries the granular `local-network` or
+`loopback-network` permission, then requests the resource only after submission.
+Unsupported permission queries fall back to a user-initiated connection attempt.
+Browsers without Local Network Access support may block HTTP endpoints from HTTPS;
+use an HTTPS local endpoint in that case.
+
+The target service must support standard CORS and allow the website's origin
+with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. No server proxy is used: localhost always
+refers to the user's computer. Requests omit credentials and reject redirects.
+Browser permission remains under the user's control.
+
+Top-level same-origin access uses the default `self` permissions policy. If this
+site is embedded, its HTTPS host must delegate `local-network; loopback-network`
+through the iframe's `allow` attribute and permit the site's origin in any
+`Permissions-Policy` header. A hosting policy that disables these features must
+be updated at the HTTP server; an HTML meta tag cannot override it.
+
+Run `node --test local-network.test.mjs` for automated connection-flow checks.
